Commands to run the backend server:

## Start the Backend Server

**Start all services (PostgreSQL, Redis, API):**
```bash
cd E:\D\Portfolio\calling_app\backend
docker-compose up -d
```

**Start only the API service:**
```bash
cd E:\D\Portfolio\calling_app\backend
docker-compose up -d api
```

## Run Database Migrations

**After starting the services, run migrations:**
```bash
cd E:\D\Portfolio\calling_app\backend
docker-compose exec api ./main migrate
```

## Useful Management Commands

**View server logs:**
```bash
docker-compose logs -f api
```

**Restart the server:**
```bash
docker-compose restart api
```

**Stop the server:**
```bash
docker-compose stop api
```

**Stop all services:**
```bash
docker-compose down
```

**Check server status:**
```bash
docker-compose ps
```

**Rebuild and restart (after code changes):**
```bash
docker-compose up -d --build api
```

## Quick Start (Complete Setup)

```bash
# Navigate to backend directory
cd E:\D\Portfolio\calling_app\backend

# Start all services
docker-compose up -d

# Run migrations
docker-compose exec api ./main migrate

# View logs to confirm it's running
docker-compose logs -f api
```

The server will be available at `http://localhost:8080` once started.